{
 "result": "I built maze.py, a level-by-level BFS over a flattened grid that returns the shortest 4-neighbour path length from S to E, or -1. It prints 4 on a small 3x3 example and -1 on a blocked 2x2 example, both as expected. gen.py builds the 2000x2000 maze with seed 7 and 28% walls. On that maze maze.py prints -1 in about 1.3 s, so the \"fast\" requirement is met only by that timing. I registered an assay that scores 1/runtime (baseline 6.6, noise 1.6%). I ran no variants, so the code is unoptimised. Verification is weak: no reachable path was checked on the large maze, and there was no cross-check against a second implementation.",
